5498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2a" :db/id 17592186422573} {:answer/id #uuid "83a40b84-ecfa-5021-a42b-e199ea1bf4ad" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2b-1" :db/id 17592186422586} {:answer/id #uuid "f8fd5393-0ed5-5c9c-b0d4-4b79be985d84" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2b" :db/id 17592186422679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8fd5393-0ed5-5c9c-b0d4-4b79be985d84" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2b" :db/id 17592186422679} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0a3bf59-d91f-5503-a55b-862d352c357f" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id 17592186422731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a900dfd-856d-5811-8760-0f71bf80c4d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-184231" :question/problem "Prove that if $n$ is odd, then $3n+5$ is even.\n\nIf $n$ is odd, then $n=\\,${{field-1}} for {{field-2}}.\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+5 & ={{field-3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $b=$ {{field-4}}. Since $a$ is {{field-5}}, we have that $b$ is {{field-6}}.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+5 & ={{field-7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a multiple of $2.$ Therefore, $3n+5$ is {{field-8}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- If an integer $n$ is even, then there exists an integer $p$ such that $n=2p.$\n\n- If an integer $n$ is odd, then there exists an integer $q$ such that $n=2q+1.$\n\nIn this case, we need to prove the following:\n\n$$\nn\\text{ is odd}\\,⇒\\,3n+5\\text{ is even}\n$$\n\nWe start by using the fact that $n$ is odd.\n\nIf $n$ is odd, then $n=2a+1$ for some integer $a.$\n\nThe idea is to substitute $n=2a+1$ into the expression $3n+5$ and show it is even by writing it as a multiple of $2.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+5 & =3(2a+1)+5 \\\\  & =6a+3+5 \\\\  & =6a+8 \\\\  & =2{{(3a+4)}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we define another integer $b=3a+4$ (highlighted above), we have that $3n+5=2b,$ which shows that $3n+5$ is indeed a multiple of $2.$\n\nLet $b=3a+4.$ Since $a$ is an integer, we have that $b$ is an integer. \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+5 & =2{{(3a+4)}_{⏟}}_{b} \\\\  & =2b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a multiple of $2.$\n\nFinally, we write our conclusion.\n\nTherefore, $3n+5$ is even."} {:db/id 17592186157673 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186157234 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91fbae70-a75d-58e4-a847-e52d9c25cb59" :knowledge-point/title "Proving a Trivial or Vacuous Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7c3d04d-cfaf-57db-a1bb-e36f3287ad2c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "nis even" :db/id 17592186154508} {:answer/id #uuid "bbcdaa04-1abd-5515-9076-2b276f307944" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mid n \\mid > - 1" :db/id 17592186154509}] :answer-field/id #uuid "033211e0-c2de-538e-930f-1a484b9600c2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id 17592186154507} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04f664d7-ef4d-5f71-bfda-0f9f6cca45e8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "nis even" :db/id 17592186154511} {:answer/id #uuid "4f5c31b0-ea8c-5332-bed0-44d5cd849978" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\mid n \\mid > - 1" :db/id 17592186154512}] :answer-field/id #uuid "be0af8b8-a407-562e-8671-a77bf4dd0a1d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id 17592186154510} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d982b1aa-9734-502d-b02c-2e11f04bae66" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.typ