/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id 17592186396372} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab5d3c4f-33de-5eef-8ae7-7817054b32b2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id 17592186396379} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb05416-e870-500e-9a56-00e679e530ba" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id 17592186396380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbb05416-e870-500e-9a56-00e679e530ba" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id 17592186396380} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd4e31a3-2c33-5488-8129-ccd3b7edb5c9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id 17592186396378} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "168810da-b39a-596e-97d5-9d3f2cee753e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the absorption property" :db/id 17592186396382} {:answer/id #uuid "5191241f-ad91-527c-9c7d-fd7612a78fdd" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the constant multiple property" :db/id 17592186396383} {:answer/id #uuid "8e35eb45-ae11-5d49-8ed6-d440fcdf4c3f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the sum property" :db/id 17592186396384} {:answer/id #uuid "047e1746-629c-5d4a-bc0b-01f3e0f827c5" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property" :db/id 17592186396385} {:answer/id #uuid "3beef058-c56a-5a74-a72d-b0d8e2526d6a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id 17592186396386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3beef058-c56a-5a74-a72d-b0d8e2526d6a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the reflexive property" :db/id 17592186396386} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2436d9b-713f-53b8-9755-f99ff60b4717" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id 17592186396381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "189a55f5-72ee-590d-b213-1f6bb96fbc77" :question/math-academy-id "q-334685" :question/problem "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)=3{e}^{2x}+2x,$ then $f=O({e}^{2x})$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below\n\n $\\text{L1}:\\,f=O(3{e}^{2x}+2x)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{2x}{3{e}^{2x}})=0$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,2x=O(3{e}^{2x})$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,f=O(3{e}^{2x})$  \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O({e}^{2x})$ \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from lines \n{{field-2}} and \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line {{field-4}}  and \n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation. \n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property. \n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen \n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\nf=O({{3{e}^{2x}+2x}_{⏟}}_{f})\n$$\n\nand this is true by $\\text{the reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ From line $\\text{L1},$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(3{e}^{2x}+2x)\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L3},$ we have\n\n$$\n2x=O(3{e}^{2x}).\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\text{L1 and L3}$ and the $\\text{absorption property},$ we have \n\n$$\nf=O(3{e}^{2x}+2x)=O(3{e}^{2x}).\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line $\\text{L4},$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(3{e}^{2x})\n$$\n\nand by the $\\text{constant multiple property}$ with $c=3,$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O({e}^{2x}).\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186157779 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186157232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4d348b-1703-51a1-be05-2e66295cacaa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Trivial Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad486718-90fd-5e9e-9943-9c86b1e6e1e4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186477443} {:answer/id #uuid "41dc14f9-6472-581d-834c-b92f0b3b2bd1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186477444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad486718-90fd-5e9e-9943-9c86b1e6e1e4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186477443} :answer-field/id #uuid "2df7f439-9445-5270-ae1a-891e7120f5d2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186477691} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b060754-d061-59ec-a9a4-7d3e81891ba6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186477445} {:answer/id #uuid "fbcd7196-0244-50a4-8bdb-048788557e77" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 175921864