{1}+{y}_{2} &=-36.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=7$ and ${y}_{2}=34.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 34\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id 17592186241143 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16476909-e6dc-5b18-955e-cfd718795ed4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186238244} {:answer/id #uuid "4583c04a-e2ab-52e7-81fb-8167f1190e1f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186238655} {:answer/id #uuid "6fc567a9-e712-50f6-afe2-c4eb98f78983" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186239020} {:answer/id #uuid "c2f9e2ec-06fa-5186-8c2c-78d345e623f1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186239770} {:answer/id #uuid "f1587271-3166-56b5-ab38-216dbdf949f7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186240187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fc567a9-e712-50f6-afe2-c4eb98f78983" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186239020} :answer-field/id #uuid "9292d405-3038-578e-a25a-a947fe32a344" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186240586}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aaf9d0f9-4c8f-533a-91f4-6216848a3e03" :question/math-academy-id "q-105928" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=-7 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=3 \\\\ 3{y}_{2}+{y}_{3} &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =-7, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =3+{y}_{1} \\\\  & =3+(-7) \\\\  & =-4, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =3-3{y}_{2} \\\\  & =3-3(-4) \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id 17592186241144 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3721f084-e142-5f33-baa4-f1483ad8f031" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 16 \\\\ -23\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186238533} {:answer/id #uuid "7792733b-cca3-5632-a467-f04ba2ce6d0b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186239087} {:answer/id #uuid "7e797d6d-322e-55f6-9562-6057b788f863" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186239155} {:answer/id #uuid "a4a111c4-fc76-59c9-ae42-fc127091245d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186239483} {:answer/id #uuid "e1791bdd-9f67-5cb2-8e6c-a0895f1b851c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186240034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3721f084-e142-5f33-baa4-f1483ad8f031" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 16 \\\\ -23\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186238533} :answer-field/id #uuid "1267ab7e-a947-5495-96a5-cfc2042f7e77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186240358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f817b0d9-deca-51e1-aedb-860b4e44d9bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-105930" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=-2 \\\\ 9{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ -4{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}+{y}_{3} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =-2, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-2-9{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-2-9(-2) \\\\  & =16, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =1+4{y}_{1}-{y}_{2} \\\\  & =1+4(-2)-(16) \\\\  & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 16 \\\\ -23\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id 17592186241145 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fa9fbb8-b2bc-5c93-bb07-bc8c7ef7c115" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Solution of an Intermediate System Using the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "253c5bec-a5e7-5fe4-8936-ee84f06ad2cd" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 70 \\\\ 80\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186238380} {:answer/id #uuid "3431ca67-1154-5315-a55d-30d8b6ec10fd" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -63 \\\\ 81\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186238506} {:answer/id #uuid "5467b34d-2f1e-5c78-85dd-2b5382f7e7be" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -56 \\\\ 80\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186238782} {:answer/id #uuid "b152e191-5d18-598f-a23e-0286d0d7f786" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 56 \\\\ -80\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186239602} {:answer/id #uuid "c8674c02-d35b-548c-9f92-7fdac92d42e1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -70 \\\\ 80\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186239819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5467b34d-2f1e-5c78-85dd-2b5382f7e7be" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -56 \\\\ 80\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186238782} :answer-field/id #uuid "697b8f6f-9b78-510a-bdce-c0f202963523" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186240524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "90586eea-75b4-50dc-8971-26e34a9a2816" :question/math-academy-id "q-105934" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=9 \\\\ 7{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=7 \\\\ -9{y}_{1}+{y}_{3} &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =9, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =7-7{y}_{1} \\\\  & =7-7(9) \\\\  & =-56, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =-1+9{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-1+9(9) \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -56 \\\\ 80\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id 17592186241146 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16cfc4d9-e678-5d11-a711-f03b27d03ba7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id 17592186238251} {:answer/id #uuid "48196e4d-5923-5fc3-ba09-551bba37a5f7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id 17592186238683} {:answer/id #uuid "764a88ed-d42b-5e8e-b7e6-0154d79ebcb8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id 17592186239076} {:answer/id #uuid "9c69f59a-92c5-5712-8d12-87a782265e35" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id 17592186239415} {:answer/id #uuid "a7a8dd22-491e-5bf2-8293-73bb146e224b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186239509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7a8dd22-491e-5bf2-8293-73bb146e224b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186239509} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0090a32-0dee-5d9f-b495-d9dbbf4db605" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186240613}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b76bf109-a8c3-51c0-a007-3381911cc6e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-105951" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{2}\\cdot {y}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=b=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=6 \\\\ 4{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=20.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=6$ and ${y}_{2}=-4.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=y=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=6 \\\\ 4{x}_{2} &=-4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{2}\\cdot {y}_{2}=(-1)\\cdot (-4)=4.$"} {:db/id 17592186241147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7634b3ac-f9e6-514e-87ba-e78590c9fa53" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 Linear System Using LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22f6367b-84f5-5b47-a09a-aa8de2644b8f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{7}" :db/id 17592186238362} {:answer/id #uuid "813327d9-1832-51ef-84d1-00133e2f63a1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id 17592186239176} {:answer/id #uuid "8e93b878-423d-5080-a191-f592c8e25cbb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{130}{7}" :db/id 17592186239293} {:answer/id #uuid "b7069b81-e348-5968-b6ae-a411b5b35221" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id 17592186239649} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc34193-52f9-5bb0-a06a-5f9897960a24" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id 17592186239856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7069b81-e348-5968-b6ae-a411b5b35221" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id 17592186239649} :answer-field/id #uuid "54336a57-2806-5ed6-bb5d-a86bbfed1d7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186240485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "68b89d00-e814-5d60-8ff8-bbe1b29f01fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-105953" :question/problem "Consider the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ and the vector $b,$ given by\n\n$$\nA={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}{{\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $⟨{x}_{1},{x}_{2}⟩$ and $⟨{y}_{1},{y}_{2}⟩$ are the solutions to the systems $Ax=b$ and $Ly=b$ respectively, what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}Ly &=b \\\\ Ux &=y.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the two systems in turn.\n\n- First, we solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=b=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} &=5 \\\\ -2{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} &=4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=5$ and ${y}_{2}=14.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\ny=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- Next, we solve $Ux=y.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=y=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ -2{x}_{2} &=14.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${x}_{2}=-7$ and ${x}_{1}=\\frac{26}{7}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{26}{7} \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {y}_{2}=\\frac{26}{7}\\cdot 14=52.$"} {:db/id 17592186243945 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119853 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c1a562-1b3d-5180-9fef-e20ea916b17a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying LU Factorizations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56258d8c-e646-509a-8f28-9b491b3481fc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461455} {:answer/id #uuid "09ef23d4-862d-578f-b427-bbae133ead4a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461456}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09ef23d4-862d-578f-b427-bbae133ead4a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461456} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b2d6e88-66be-55b8-937a-f097cf9d0a8f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186462481} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae5b49c3-0779-557c-8921-65282b453bed" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461457} {:answer/id #uuid "68c311fa-d65a-5064-a5f2-843e88a9f3f9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae5b49c3-0779-557c-8921-65282b453bed" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461457} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fdefae0-1945-5459-8e2f-89ff965eadc8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186462482} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41c731b3-dbc9-5242-b984-177958f91d5e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461459} {:answer/id #uuid "6bd0f37d-448b-5552-acb3-dff3d5f8c125" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41c731b3-dbc9-5242-b984-177958f91d5e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461459} :answer-field/id #uuid "4715c2ce-c869-5eb5-8141-1dcbba399ac8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186462483}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae199b8f-96fc-541b-8e00-25e26e1c8f40" :question/math-academy-id "q-106751" :question/problem "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $A?$\n- **I.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **II.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **III.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that in the LU factorization of a matrix $A,$ we write $A=LU$ where the matrix $L$ is a unit lower triangular matrix (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:\n\n$$\nA=\\overset{L}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 1\\end{bmatrix}}}\\cdot \\overset{U}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}}}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The second product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the left is not a unit lower triangular matrix, as its main diagonal contains a number not equal to $1.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The third product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the right is not an upper triangular matrix, as it has a non-zero entry below the diagonal.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id 17592186243947 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119853 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2c1a562-1b3d-5180-9fef-e20ea916b17a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying LU Factorizations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe57a78b-d4ad-58a3-a332-1d5d1a41161f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461461} {:answer/id #uuid "ed276dc2-e752-5149-8daa-6a78dac6eb3c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe57a78b-d4ad-58a3-a332-1d5d1a41161f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461461} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ad862c7-06d6-5d3e-9df8-9dc54efcf0c4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186462484} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "553c272d-3d3a-5260-bd9f-714a8605af98" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461463} {:answer/id #uuid "4e234d92-1a15-5982-80b2-1a67952674f1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e234d92-1a15-5982-80b2-1a67952674f1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461464} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a44ba0a-420a-5ce8-9090-7717c7cae446" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186462485} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2f54ad7-e111-5f33-a28c-2b1e1910a1da" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461465} {:answer/id #uuid "90d8b03d-a3ca-513c-a593-4303a50bda9a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90d8b03d-a3ca-513c-a593-4303a50bda9a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461466} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7e2bb08-94b2-5ba1-8d6a-ae59c5114f74" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186462486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02d764cc-1d89-57be-9543-a3cb1c6ba444" :question/math-academy-id "q-106756" :question/problem "Which of the following products is the LU factorization of a matrix $A?$\n- **I.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **II.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\n- **III.** $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that in the LU factorization of a matrix $A,$ we write $A=LU$ where the matrix $L$ is a unit lower triangular matrix (a lower triangular matrix that has only $1$'s on the main diagonal) and the matrix $U$ is an upper triangular matrix:\n\n$$\nA=\\overset{L}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & 1\\end{bmatrix}}}\\cdot \\overset{U}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}}}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each product in turn.\n\n- The first product is *not* in $LU$ form because the matrix on the left is not a unit lower triangular matrix, as its main diagonal contains a number not equal to $1.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The second product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The third product is in $LU$ form because the left matrix is a unit lower triangular matrix, and the right matrix is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."} {:db/id 17592186243948 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119792 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9279d979-74ba-5504-b98a-63692db3af72" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e37e6cc-fad6-5510-9620-2cbac7ce22f7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id 17592186241439} {:answer/id #uuid "8ba5c239-540d-5f86-ac6d-97caed8a3faf" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id 17592186242416} {:answer/id #uuid "8bab7e05-3097-50f9-97ae-0da4430bb726" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id 17592186242417} {:answer/id #uuid "8eefa27a-e9ae-567c-9c88-944a22b88b15" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-35" :db/id 17592186242437} {:answer/id #uuid "a2d916f4-e1c3-59c3-b962-73fcbf193360" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id 17592186242604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ba5c239-540d-5f86-ac6d-97caed8a3faf" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id 17592186242416} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7fbcc62-56cc-5358-9e7d-035227d1830e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186243840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e43d37a-2ce4-531c-9855-25d3d30a5758" :question/math-academy-id "q-106762" :question/problem "Given that\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 15 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$ \nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU$, then ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{22}=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 15 & -4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}{{\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${l}_{21}=-5,{u}_{22}=6,$ and ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{12}=-30.$"} {:db/id 17592186243949 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119792 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9279d979-74ba-5504-b98a-63692db3af72" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03ddb432-c159-51bd-87f7-46377395435b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186241213} {:answer/id #uuid "797c91c1-9cd0-58dd-9630-d65ae8a82a3f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186242251} {:answer/id #uuid "95236878-0d84-5730-9210-7d52e16f2f34" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186242488} {:answer/id #uuid "abfe08e7-1a8e-53cd-a0cc-09d44eab6540" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186242683} {:answer/id #uuid "e313faa3-97f4-5d01-bd42-efbcd8a6d8df" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186243200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "797c91c1-9cd0-58dd-9630-d65ae8a82a3f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186242251} :answer-field/id #uuid "491415e0-0ac3-5791-b266-069f3eb88034" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186243576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bd4d8bf8-4a33-530d-bc80-05a910fd04f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-106763" :question/problem "Given that \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -7 \\\\ -12 & 18\\end{bmatrix}$ \nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU,$ then $L=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -7 \\\\ -12 & 18\\end{bmatrix} & \\,{R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}{{\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186243950 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119792 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9279d979-74ba-5504-b98a-63692db3af72" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the LU Factorization of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00fcd0e3-1b06-5b0d-8ec5-bdcb973e0121" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186241193} {:answer/id #uuid "2f21bf4f-8fb6-51cb-b46d-2704e33c0f5d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186241597} {:answer/id #uuid "6459af2f-a6b5-563c-b06a-268a7964e5fb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186242083} {:answer/id #uuid "a7a1a69e-9cf6-54d9-af78-f001be097a2b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186242650} {:answer/id #uuid "e0db43ec-63a9-52d8-940d-22db7f0c0613" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186243178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0db43ec-63a9-52d8-940d-22db7f0c0613" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186243178} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfca5d8f-a9c0-5b49-923e-17f332033246" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186243804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #