g the LU Factorization Using a Single Elementary Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0857eda5-eeea-55ef-98f6-53654c385d86" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186241250} {:answer/id #uuid "1ec430f7-7c2f-5509-bf32-e90bd49e5ba1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186241448} {:answer/id #uuid "854a3cea-9af5-57ca-889a-18380bc93538" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186242345} {:answer/id #uuid "c660c215-abc4-52f5-b033-211ea838c77a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186242931} {:answer/id #uuid "d2d3c330-b131-5fd2-aab2-d93803cd3b71" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186243038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "854a3cea-9af5-57ca-889a-18380bc93538" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186242345} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbad9009-e489-5ede-8b72-2d149df4990c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186243820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b0b89e6-144c-5b9b-accd-ae485d790cb9" :question/math-academy-id "q-106836" :question/problem "Given that \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU,$ then $L=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -6 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} & ⟺ & \\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}{{\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186243965 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119795 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c91fb2b-5607-555d-b897-f0e76765dfa6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Lower Triangular Matrix Given the Elementary Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25f20815-d3c9-5266-a9ea-efd0b9f40481" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186241507} {:answer/id #uuid "2a100052-8c46-523f-bb66-e7fb58725152" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186241553} {:answer/id #uuid "87c84f1b-05b2-5fb4-86d5-ac25913dcef9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186242370} {:answer/id #uuid "b8332ebc-6831-5216-9726-52979fa52de5" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186242797} {:answer/id #uuid "fa11afd4-5218-5cf8-a73f-47d278eaf0a6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186243382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87c84f1b-05b2-5fb4-86d5-ac25913dcef9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186242370} :answer-field/id #uuid "56764b89-1d6b-5b0e-a256-bd88b558bbc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186243611}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8bcf5266-c07e-506f-ad28-ce8fd193bd74" :question/math-academy-id "q-106843" :question/problem "Suppose that a $3\\times 3$ matrix $C$ is reduced to row echelon form using the following elementary row operations, applied in the order in which they appear:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+9{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nGiven that $C$ has the LU factorization $C=LU,$ then $L=$" :question/worked-solution "Applying ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1}$ and then ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+9\\cdot {R}_{1}$ is equivalent to multiplying $C$ from the left by the following elementary matrices:\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{E}_{2}}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{E}_{1}}\\cdot C=U\n$$\n\nNow, since ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}C=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{2}$ and ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}C & =U \\\\ {E}_{1}C & ={E}_{2}^{-1}U \\\\ C & ={E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}^{-1}U \\\\ C & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}U \\\\ C & =(\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix})U \\\\ C & ={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot U\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186243966 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119795 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c91fb2b-5607-555d-b897-f0e76765dfa6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Lower Triangular Matrix Given the Elementary Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3344b786-674b-5fd2-9d29-837e625aa501" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186241632} {:answer/id #uuid "80dafbab-27c8-576b-b2ce-69b8b080bf51" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186242309} {:answer/id #uuid "83bafad9-1114-5e06-bd66-d793c74a86bb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186242334} {:answer/id #uuid "9bd15dac-4809-5f03-aa6a-8f97384065ce" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186242541} {:answer/id #uuid "e7d50e5f-77de-5893-ac67-36ccb6d71066" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 &