pe/checkbox} :db/id 17592186462546}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1069f3ce-ee29-5917-b7ea-2041ea76b45b" :question/math-academy-id "q-109525" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $v$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $v$ is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1$ of $A$\n\nII. $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1$ of $A$\n\nIII. $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1$ of $A$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A *generalized eigenvector* ${v}_{n}$ of rank $n$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda $ of a matrix $A$ is a nonzero vector such that\n\n$$\n{v}_{n}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{n-1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }…\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\nwhere ${v}_{n-1},{v}_{n-2},…,{v}_{1}\\ne 0.$ An *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$\n\nFirst, we compute $A-I:$\n\n$$\nA-I=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the image of $v$ under the action of $A-I:$\n\n$$\n(A-I)v=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}={{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{w}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Since we got a nonzero vector in the last step, we now compute the image of $w$ under the action of $A-I:$\n\n$$\n(A-I)w=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{v}\\overset{A-I\\,}{\\to }{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{w}\\overset{A-I\\,}{\\to }{{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A-I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $2$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id 17592186247011 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186152226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "76e60bc4-ae61-5c39-ad80-14e0cdab14da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Generalized Eigenvectors of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d454755c-f070-50aa-a288-101e2c21d000" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461587} {:answer/id #uuid "30ee683c-53a6-59f7-8be2-89adc86a0928" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d454755c-f070-50aa-a288-101e2c21d000" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461587} :answer-field/id #uuid "e523968e-1140-5585-9eb5-1cada8f2087f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186462547} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac2feef2-eec5-563a-98ee-39b6c228a14e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186461589} {:answer/id #uuid "36f7130e-dbc8-5e7d-9ccd-5df6d1e55ba9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186461590}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac2feef2-eec5-563a-98ee