| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}_{2}$ | **$7$** | **$5$** | **$17$** | **$20$** | **$30$** |\n| $y$ | $-11$ | $-4$ | $6$ | $12$ | $20$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the plane $y={\\beta }_{1}{x}_{1}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}_{2}$ that best fits the data above can be found using multiple linear regression as \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| ${x}_{1}$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}_{2}$ | **$7$** | **$5$** | **$17$** | **$20$** | **$30$** |\n| $y$ | $-11$ | $-4$ | $6$ | $12$ | $20$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the plane \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{1}{x}_{1}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}_{2}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 17 \\\\ 4 & 20 \\\\ 5 & 30\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{bmatrix}}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."} {:db/id 17592186271971 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186133809 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eaee4e9-7be5-5c35-bc88-89697a15d75a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements of a Multiple Linear Regression That Passes Through the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02104dc9-cf44-5d95-a1fa-2301b23565f1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 30 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 15 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 20 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 15 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 12\\end{bmatrix}" :d