 Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "081a40c5-551f-580d-b01c-1d60d32cb060" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id 17592186342306} {:answer/id #uuid "0d73c50f-626b-5a8e-a458-314c34867174" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186342352} {:answer/id #uuid "1f356320-8189-5405-b803-d0029934a836" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}" :db/id 17592186342496} {:answer/id #uuid "d3020996-e213-5e09-92b5-f8f81fe30866" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186344088} {:answer/id #uuid "f7b57cbb-63bc-5327-8a0a-50b2fe957a22" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id 17592186344420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3020996-e213-5e09-92b5-f8f81fe30866" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186344088} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe5461c8-51c8-5591-bfc3-b3c528e3db44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186344937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "32d360b2-b07c-58ea-8316-13ed526cce1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-75978" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,-8\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,4\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}+{{(\\,2\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{3}}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{3}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=-8\\cdot {b}_{1}+4\\cdot {b}_{2}+2\\cdot {b}_{3}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{2}=4.$"} {:db/id 17592186345152 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119859 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2926764-dfbc-5e4e-a6b0-db24a7298a64" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of a Vector Relative To a Given Basis by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38af80af-d49d-54b5-aaac-e804ec8c572f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}" :db/id 17592186342704} {:answer/id #uuid "599365f9-b07b-5a51-90c6-591c6ef0676c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id 17592186342989} {:answer/id #uuid "6f11f370-7154-5e9c-a4e9-b57216fdc44b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id 17592186343195} {:answer/id #uuid "7661a5d2-790d-560a-bb3e-426238e8cf3e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id 17592186343264} {:answer/id #uuid "891b0ab7-d32f-5dea-abb7-0b327f3d717c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186343426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "599365f9-b07b-5a51-90c6-591c6ef0676c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id 17592186342989} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ae94580-b08e-514f-af33-6d3e14d4f24e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186344762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4061dc6a-87c8-53d1-aa6a-18325afc93ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-75984" :question/problem "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{b}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of ${x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,-2\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,-1\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}+{{(\\,5\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{3}}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{3}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=-2\\cdot {b}_{1}+(-1)\\cdot {b}_{2}+5\\cdot {b}_{3}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{3}=5.$"} {:db/id 17592186345161 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186152168 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "689f9f44-4776-56a7-915f-d0dab0755002" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bdc00c7-d8aa-5cc7-a0a7-e8061f0c4597" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id 17592186342343} {:answer/id #uuid "370e629d-7450-5b57-a85f-8d0196bbea84" :answer/type {:db/id 175921860