-field/id #uuid "4c5f53eb-60e0-5636-a955-f574b8536172" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id 17592186379022}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fc4b578b-6250-5651-a423-a5ab765ad427" :question/math-academy-id "q-175912" :question/problem "$$\n{{3\\,|\\,9}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{3\\,|\\,16}_{⏟}}_{B}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $A$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $B$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $A∧B$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is true, and $B$ is false. Therefore, the result is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{3\\,|\\,9}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{3\\,|\\,16}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{true}∧\\text{false}≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186379025 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186054641 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93bc0caa-2352-5d02-9ccf-7267dff4be2c" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Compound Statements in Symbolic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aff03dac-1a8f-5dbf-a4f8-9d2fef0ad08f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∧" :db/id 17592186379027} {:answer/id #uuid "4e321d34-1455-5152-bc41-3a72d41cfaa4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R" :db/id 17592186379028} {:answer/id #uuid "be75db87-a664-505d-b84d-604754c38fda" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "S" :db/id 17592186379029} {:answer/id #uuid "64c60aee-9293-50b9-bd71-a3a552091fdc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident 