9-5946-bf6a-d22d986bc83e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186472190}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d9a12d6-16ca-57db-975d-02505a889530" :question/math-academy-id "q-216618" :question/problem "$$\n(\\,∀x\\in N,\\,x>{n}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{I}\\end{aligned}}+1\\,)⇒(\\,∃z\\in R,\\,{{z}^{3}}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{II}\\end{aligned}}-1={y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{III}\\end{aligned}}\\,)\n$$\n\nWhich occurrences of the variables in the expression above are free?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- Occurrence I of the variable $n$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $n.$\n\n- Occurrence II of the variable $z$ is *bound* since it lies within the scope of the quantifier $∃z$ that uses $z:$ \n\n$$\n(\\,∀x\\in N,\\,x>n+1\\,)⇒(\\,∃z\\in R,\\,\\overset{\\text{scope of }∃z}{\\overset{⏞}{{z}^{3}-1={y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}}}\\,)\n$$\n\n- Occurrence III of the variable $y$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $y.$\n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\,∀{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in N,\\,{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}>{n}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}+1\\,)⇒(\\,∃{z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in R,\\,{{z}^{3}}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}-1={y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ ↑ \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}\\,)\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrence is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id 17592186381942 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186162042 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6732620-fad1-5dd3-98c5-07ba59d0b286" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Factor in the SVD of a Rectangular Matrix: Advanced Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3deee69f-3a09-5221-985a-bd0ac7deae81" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id 17592186381944} {:answer/id #uuid "9063686e-f6d9-5985-ab01-efb95a0f5ea0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id 17592186381945} {:answer/id #uuid "8b544ef9-20fe-5f86-891a-be7f8bae3513" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id 17592186381946} {:answer/id #uuid "6536ef14-8e86-50c8-955d-af6af6b6f266" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186381947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b544ef9-20fe-5f86-891a-be7f8bae3513" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id 17592186381946} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9d9d60e-4182-57e9-b60d-64d8685d7b9c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id 17592186381943} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58a1695d-6094-5723-bf78-2ec73a2b0e60" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id 17592186381949} {:answer/id #uuid "a8370bdd-a24f-5673-b50b-db9eb1fb6f15" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id 17592186381950} {:answer/id #uuid "4bcb16a4-50c2-5e53-a3bb-8da59f429f54" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id 17592186381951} {:answer/id #uuid "b6e12a4a-2d32-51a7-b723-7c82e62bde90" :answer/type {:d