"1" :db/id 17592186381978} {:answer/id #uuid "1b3aa4df-c12b-5303-9a18-70ab969b2071" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id 17592186381979} {:answer/id #uuid "85194c7e-64e5-50fa-8bee-4c95bce0b225" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186381980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b3aa4df-c12b-5303-9a18-70ab969b2071" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id 17592186381979} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a14992c-e74a-57bc-b5d3-971af49a4001" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id 17592186381976} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d958d8f-4c27-5aac-ab58-a51ea07a1058" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}" :db/id 17592186381982} {:answer/id #uuid "8f660977-f61e-5600-9e89-c7a9d4e32cba" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{2}" :db/id 17592186381983} {:answer/id #uuid "7d64fecc-0d4d-5720-bfef-5cc7873da9be" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}_{2}" :db/id 17592186381984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f660977-f61e-5600-9e89-c7a9d4e32cba" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{2}" :db/id 17592186381983} :answer-field/id #uuid "8da00724-323d-5f3d-8ac2-51e5ef2ad260" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id 17592186381981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d47baabf-d20b-51dc-ba6e-5b8ddf2ee3e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-363830" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ \\,\\,-1 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{10} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$  select the correct options in the computations of the matrix $U$ below.\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce the singular values ${\\sigma }_{1}=\\sqrt{10}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0.$\n\nNow, we compute the $1$st column of $U.$ It is given by:\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${u}_{1}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n|  |  | $0$ |  |  |\n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, and we do not have the third singular value, we can't use the same formula to find the second and third columns of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal.\n\nHence, we must find vectors $u=[{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}]^{T}$ such that ${u}_{1}\\cdot u=0,$ which is equivalent to \n\n$$\n{{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nChoosing ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ as free variables, the general solution is given by:\n\n|  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-5}} |  |  |\n|  |  | ${x}_{3}$ |  |  |\n\nthat we can rewrite as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}={x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the two linearly independent solutions are already mutually orthogonal, we only need to normalize them. Hence, we obtain the second and third columns of $U:$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"40px\">\n                ${u}_{2}=\\,\\,$\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"90px\">\n                {{field-6}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n                {{field-7}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"40px\">\n                ${u}_{3}=\\,\\,$\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"90px\">\n                $0$\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n                {{field-8}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n                {{field-9}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if  $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $3\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n- $Σ$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix with nonnegative elements on the main diagonal and zeroes outside the main diagonal,\n\n- $U$ is an orthogonal $3\\times 3$ matrix,\n\n- $V$ is an orthogonal $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=\\sqrt{10}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0.$\nAlso, the columns ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ of $V$ give us the right singular vectors of $A.$\n\nTherefore, we can compute the first column of $U$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, and we do not have the third singular value, we can't use the same formula to find the second and third columns of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find vectors \n\n$$\nu=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nsuch that ${u}_{1}\\cdot u=0$ and $‖u‖=1.$\n\nSolving ${u}_{1}\\cdot u=0,$ which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{x}_{1}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{x}_{2}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=0,\n$$\n\nwe get the general solution \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}={x}_{2}{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{x}_{3}{{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are free variables.\n\nNotice that the two linearly independent solutions ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ are mutually orthogonal. Therefore, we only need to normalize them. This gives the second and third columns of $U:$   \n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,{u}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the matrix $U$ could be the following:\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186381985 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186162042 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6732620-fad1-5dd3-98c5-07ba59d0b286" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Factor in the SVD of a Rectangular Matrix: Advanced Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "289d908e-d458-5cbf-8048-b0dfd91442e6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id 17592186381987} {:answer/id #uuid "90a4e820-0a7c-5a7c-b02e-659f45da5434" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id 17592186381988} {:answer/id #uuid "2bb67b59-9e97-582f-9f02-a93928b17b9b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id 17592186381989} {:answer/id #uuid "8e51a986-b985-5601-944e-d9d27343f36d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186381990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "289d908e-d458-5cbf-8048-b0dfd91442e6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id 17592186381987} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa4283c3-c6f2-5b69-9abf-b4d9e48bc36e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id 17592186381986} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbc70a3a-c1bc-504e-ba29-0648b22dfa6e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{3}" :db/id 17592186381992} {:answer/id #uuid "82c8ab8c-9496-537f-9b50-fa45d1cd6a4c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{2}" :db/id 17592186381993} {:answer/id #uuid "1c1588b1-fcd0-5121-9d08-ba8f90ebc1f2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{2}" :db/id 17592186381994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82c8ab8c-9496-537f-9b50-fa45d1cd6a4c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{2}" :db/id 17592186381993} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0beffd5-07c5-5223-8686-da966c2ce057" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id 17592186381991} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fd7ff6c-0181-5703-be56-4bb