 {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ba9ef88d-4295-592b-9071-b4477cb43227" :question/math-academy-id "q-216054" :question/problem "Let $x\\in Q.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ If $______,$ then $|x+3|<8.$ \n\nWhich of the following could be placed into the blank space above to create a statement whose proof is vacuous?\n- **I.** $\\sqrt{5}\\in R$\n- **II.** ${cos}^{2}⁡x>1$\n- **III.** $3x+2>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that an implication has a *vacuous proof* if the antecedent is always false: \n\n$$\n\\overset{\\text{Always false}}{\\overset{⏞}{P}}⇒\\,Q\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the consequent is true or false. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our antecedents in turn.\n\n- Statement I is always true. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate II, defined for $x\\in Q,$ is always false. $\\,✓$\n\n- Predicate III, defined for $x\\in Q,$ is *not* always false. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id 17592186384751 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186157234 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91fbae70-a75d-58e4-a847-e52d9c25cb59" :knowledge-point/title "Proving a Trivial or Vacuous Statement"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "659e1c9d-ea33-588f-8e94-8b05a833e6d9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{m}^{2}-8m<-16" :db/id 17592186384753} {:answer/id #uuid "93b05afd-2fbf-5df1-a701-3a2bbfcc8416" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "m\\le -4" :db/id 17592186384754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "659e1c9d-ea33-588f-8e94-8b05a833e6d9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{m}^{2}-8m<-16" :db/id 17592186384753} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a7804ba-a472-5d00-9327-bd01516cba5f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} 