stion/id #uuid "a844a22e-b15d-5e5c-85e3-c50d8ec750ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-139651" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$3$** | **$5$** | **$7$** | **$9$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-4$ | $5$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{bmatrix}=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$3$** | **$5$** | **$7$** | **$9$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-4$ | $5$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & {1}^{2} & {1}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{2} & {3}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 5 & {5}^{2} & {5}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 7 & {7}^{2} & {7}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 9 & {9}^{2} & {9}^{3}\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{bmatrix}}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."} {:db/id 17592186400805 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186133823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa5bf185-de29-5185-ba57-c64250332dfa" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Elements of a Polynomial Regression Model"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4