constant term can be written as $3=2+1.$\n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is $\\text{odd}$ since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =6p+10q+3 \\\\  & =(6p+10q+2)+1 \\\\  & =2({{3p+5q+1}_{⏟}}_{a})+1 \\\\  & =2a+1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a=3p+5q+1\\in Z.$"} {:db/id 17592186407093 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186171928 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd14b427-db87-5c61-bcd2-4ecec58450a3" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Parity of Non-Linear Expressions With Multiple Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80db6ff3-8290-5af1-9271-34f8a4c983ed" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id 17592186407026} {:answer/id #uuid "cddf6ea8-210f-5b6d-a034-2fcb454662cc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id 17592186407049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cddf6ea8-210f-5b6d-a034-2fcb454662cc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id 17592186407049} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e425e18-ff25-58e7-bd5e-c08e391f662c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id 17592186407068} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a15e0b4-cd8e-54e4-8da9-edb1ea630a53" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2a+1" :db/id 17592186407001} {:answer/id #uuid "32918dbe-a031-5688-bd79-be4a3f4f34d1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2a" :db/id 17592186407003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32918dbe-a031-5688-bd79-be4a3f4f34d1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2a" :db/id 17592186407003} :answer-field/id #uuid "116a5308-6574-5208-983a-e1b9f840e87a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id 1