 $r$ by computing $r=a-qn.$ This gives\n\n$$\nr=88-(9)(9)=7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write $88=qn+r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}88={{9}_{⏟}}_{q}\\cdot 9+{{7}_{⏟}}_{r}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $q\\cdot r=9\\cdot 7=63.$"} {:db/id 17592186407744 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186152165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "374cafa1-c178-5125-bda0-19b4e1c51892" :knowledge-point/title "The Division Algorithm For Negative Integers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bd829d3-ee49-5c38-8c08-b6ec51134281" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id 17592186407683} {:answer/id #uuid "5d320045-3505-52c7-9b18-6ee203d791e4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id 17592186407697} {:answer/id #uuid "a6d4c72d-b3a9-5366-9277-17f8104f171a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id 17592186407713} {:answer/id #uuid "c71f8d3a-2da9-51c9-87c6-9526215b0ec4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186407718} {:answer/id #uuid "cdea4221-de0b-5bcf-8afd-ee1233a793b1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id 17592186407721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c71f8d3a-2da9-51c9-87c6-9526215b0ec4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186407718} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf6de2b2-e1ba-5267-9188-c2ceca439ab3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186407734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d7616244-dc19-5790-9506-1e0646247891" :question/math-academy-id "q-77089" :question/problem "Let $a=-36$ and $n=5.$ Find integers $q$ and $r$ such that $a=qn+r,$ where $0\\le r<n.$ Then, $r=$" :question/worked-solution "Dividing $-36$ by $5$ using integer division, we notice that\n\n$$\n-8<-36÷5<-7.\n$$\n\nThe quotient $q$ is the left-hand value. So $q=-8.$\n\nNext, we find the remainder $r$ by solving $r=a-qn.$ This gives\n\n$$\nr=-36-(-8)(5)=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write $-36=qn+r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-36={{(-8)}_{⏟}}_{q}\\cdot 5+{{4}_{⏟}}_{r}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $r=4.$"} {:db/id 17592186408019 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186162042 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6732620-fad1-5dd3-98c5-07ba59d0b286" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the First Factor in the SVD of a Rectangular Matrix: Advanced Cases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1624144f-dc91-5236-84ee-18b96e8277af" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{2}" :db/id 17592186407934} {:answer/id #uuid "1f0a89b3-42e1-5c0c-9f1d-976b0b80e3f9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}_{2}" :db/id 17592186407939} {:answer/id #uuid "746511ed-c96a-5c0b-a954-73fab4f89071" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{3}" :db/id 17592186407962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1624144f-dc91-5236-84ee-18b96e8277af" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{2}" :db/id 17592186407934} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ef2a40d-dd8f-5054-9101-9b4095ee0f14" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id 17592186408004} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e47d3ea-4750-55d7-9ad9-f144dbee61aa" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id 17592186407943} {:answer/id #uuid "9c719bc8-cc87-56ef-930a-6bf23b501c80" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id 17592186407975} {:answer/id #uuid "cea590ba-fbf3-55d0-a265-d70d43b6166d" :