nd $Q$ being congruent triangles is a **sufficient** condition for $P$ and $Q$ having the same area\n- **IV.** $P$ and $Q$ having the same area is a **sufficient** condition for $P$ and $Q$ being congruent triangles" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n{{(\\,P\\text{ and }Q\\text{ are congruent triangles}\\,)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{sufficient}}\\,⇒\\,{{(\\,P\\text{ and }Q\\text{ have the same area}\\,)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{necessary}}\n$$\n\nis a true statement. Therefore:\n\n- Statement II is true. $P$ and $Q$ having the same area is a **necessary** condition for $P$ and $Q$ being congruent triangles.\n\n- Statement III is true. $P$ and $Q$ being congruent triangles is a **sufficient** condition for $P$ and $Q$ having the same area.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id 17592186420705 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186152076 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6414abb9-00d3-55ea-a1e5-da99999c3ccc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary or Sufficient Conditions From Implications"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "249e2dff-033f-5340-b2d2-ea5b106a947b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186453648} {:answer/id #uuid "7124ea30-3bdc-5464-9843-2ce2517fcf9e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186453649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7124ea30-3bdc-5464-9843-2ce2517fcf9e" :answer/type {:db/i