answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186453655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "195487bd-bfd6-5cbd-b556-5442da419935" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186453655} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d74078e-403c-53bb-b600-78b7e20a550f" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186454577}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb9b0e1b-3e64-5482-b003-6352af7b5cae" :question/math-academy-id "q-183396" :question/problem "$\\,$ If $A⊂B,$ then $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the implication above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$ is a **necessary** condition for $A⊂B$\n- **II.** $A⊂B$ is a **necessary** condition for $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$\n- **III.** $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$ is a **sufficient** condition for $A⊂B$\n- **IV.** $A⊂B$ is a **sufficient** condition for $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n{{(\\,A⊂B\\,)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{sufficient}}\\,⇒\\,{{(\\,A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅\\,)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{necessary}}\n$$\n\nis a true statement. Therefore:\n\n- Statement I is true. $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$ is a **necessary** condition for $A⊂B.$\n\n- Statement IV is true. $A⊂B$ is a **sufficient** condition for $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\""} {:db/id 17592186421141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186198283 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c26aeaa-9252-5bd3-9ad6-0fc25ca6b03c" :knowledge-point/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "177aca68-9ef3-57f2-8782-7922f7fdcee7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474594} {:answer/id #uuid "27217023-5fb1-53d0-9a9b-49549b2e5ece" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27217023-5fb1-53d0-9a9b-49549b2e5ece" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474595} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0e62a6b-b826-5d56-826c-3f7c9ec98dea" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186475223} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2dc5cc1-7434-55bb-a406-1d1e6e254658" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474596} {:answer/id #uuid "05017e46-d244-50ca-8c96-927beaf7a0a0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2dc5cc1-7434-55bb-a406-1d1e6e254658" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474596} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d7d347b-6157-5d76-a456-77eb2150acb0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186475224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cce7b4dd-ecf5-5770-bb2b-64d8b861e198" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474598} {:answer/id #uuid "f6556b17-607c-5539-b341-8b02d501a75a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cce7b4dd-ecf5-5770-bb2b-64d8b861e198" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474598} :answer-field/id #uuid "826f982e-2d81-59a1-b8ed-73e1e4460bd5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186475225} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a88484f5-b344-5db6-b1d4-105554bbb0f4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474600} {:answer/id #uuid "ff97cc03-e2de-5d2a-b9a5-83cfca9f550f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a88484f5-b344-5db6-b1d4-105554bbb0f4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474600} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a7c415d-face-5047-bf43-5a7f46334342" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186475226}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "03f10976-674d-5f7f-9c6a-ec5de8c4e5cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-183510" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x=-1$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ $(x-1)(x+1)=0$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n- **I.** $x=-1$ is sufficient for $(x-1)(x+1)=0$\n- **II.** $x=-1$ is necessary for $(x-1)(x+1)=0$\n- **III.** For $(x-1)(x+1)=0,$ it is necessary that $x=-1$\n- **IV.** For $x=-1,$ it is sufficient that $(x-1)(x+1)=0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe have the following grammatical constructions for $S⇒N:$\n\n- $S$ is sufficient for $N$\n\n- For $N,$ it is sufficient that $S$\n\n- $N$ is necessary for $S$\n\n- For $S,$ it is necessary that $N$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n{{x=-1}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{is sufficient for}\\,{{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n{{x=-1}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{is necessary for}\\,{{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n\\text{for}\\,{{(x-1)(x+1)=0,}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{it is necessary that}\\,{{x=-1}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option IV reads\n\n$$\n\\text{for}\\,{{x=-1,}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{it is sufficient that}\\,{{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id 17592186421142 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186198282 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0809c075-e1be-5d49-b1fe-5433114bcf16" :knowledge-point/title "\"If-Then\", \"If\", \"Only If\", and \"Implies\""}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0945ef13-941d-515b-b4ae-e682b2cbe6eb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474580} {:answer/id #uuid "d9b76547-30ba-5674-aaf4-f6a21243637d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0945ef13-941d-515b-b4ae-e682b2cbe6eb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474580} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fb3d849-75e4-5708-89e8-c4fd195fa85d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186475216} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b099b78-69e8-5b08-9c8f-7877b9604ed9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474582} {:answer/id #uuid "0570949e-7425-5fb0-95d5-a3cd6859565f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b099b78-69e8-5b08-9c8f-7877b9604ed9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474582} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbb6a5ff-7a9b-5d17-a103-5773db20bbb1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186475217} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85f5f97c-ac05-5910-a741-ba015942a833" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474584} {:answer/id #uuid "e3cf666e-1401-5ea9-a173-e0abeab42ac4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85f5f97c-ac05-5910-a741-ba015942a833" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474584} :answer-field/id #uuid "8031bcc8-9793-503b-baef-a85091ae70ba" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186475218} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a358e67-66e9-5231-ae52-d2a6a5099375" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474586} {:answer/id #uuid "24a68289-9468-5c6a-a2f8-ee91ce1c5a68" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24a68289-9468-5c6a-a2f8-ee91ce1c5a68" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474587} :answer-field/id #uuid "b21175e6-3a06-52f7-895c-d02b438ccfe3" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186475219}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0e0b252f-632c-5fb4-955e-f2c2686886d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-183448" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x=2$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ ${x}^{2}=4$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n- **I.** ${x}^{2}=4$ implies $x=2$\n- **II.** If ${x}^{2}=4,$ then $x=2$\n- **III.** ${x}^{2}=4$ only if $x=2$\n- **IV.** ${x}^{2}=4$ if $x=2$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the implication $P⇒Q:$\n\n- If $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $P$ only if $Q$\n\n- $Q$ if $P$\n\n- $P$ implies $Q$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n{{{x}^{2}=4}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{implies}\\,{{x=2}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n\\text{if}\\,{{{x}^{2}=4}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)},\\,\\text{then}\\,{{x=2}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n{{{x}^{2}=4}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{only if}\\,{{x=2}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option IV reads\n\n$$\n{{{x}^{2}=4}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{if}\\,{{x=2}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"IV only.\""} {:db/id 17592186421146 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186198284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b24ae815-5706-5b65-bab8-2d67f8405c9c" :knowledge-point/title "\"Whenever\", and \"Provided That\""}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c97a67bd-0eab-522a-b912-f7d7b1965ac9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474614} {:answer/id #uuid "9e408c6c-7a9d-5fc8-8352-2e6d614fc5fe" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c97a67bd-0eab-522a-b912-f7d7b1965ac9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474614} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdba47ab-ad3c-5f97-851d-51e76579632c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186475233} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "327a00dd-4553-507d-8ed6-59817b49dc98" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474616} {:answer/id #uuid "668c2ea7-19db-5f8f-a0a1-559b819f0c5c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "327a00dd-4553-507d-8ed6-59817b49dc98" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474616} :answer-field/id #uuid "9afb0038-f0d7-57d4-aa49-f5eccca86484" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186475234} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5272c8a2-901f-5f97-b6c1-9a8da0f2647c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474618} {:answer/id #uuid "5fc7e624-31af-503c-a628-308e4e745a19" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fc7e624-31af-503c-a628-308e4e745a19" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474619} :answer-field/id #uuid "37b95fe8-12f9-57d5-b19a-d819c349b4a4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186475235}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "50849cc0-0b42-5b52-abb5-e0bdf56880ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-183568" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $0\\le x<1$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ $|x|<1$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n- **I.** Whenever $|x|<1,$ then $0\\le x<1$\n- **II.** $0\\le x<1$ whenever $|x|<1$\n- **III.** $|x|<1,$ provided that $0\\le x<1$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $P⇒Q$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- Whenever $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $Q$ whenever $P$\n\n- $Q,$ provided that $P$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n\\text{Whenever}\\,{{|x|<1}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)},\\,\\text{then}\\,{{0\\le x<1}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n{{0\\le x<1}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{whenever}\\,{{|x|<1}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n{{|x|<1\\text{,}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{provided that}\\,{{0\\le x<1}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id 17592186421148 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186198284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b24ae815-5706-5b65-bab8-2d67f8405c9c" :knowledge-point/title "\"Whenever\", and \"Provided That\""}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ec589ad-6e14-5afe-b705-86a37c1f6e8e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474602} {:answer/id #uuid "1d21f13a-49f5-5984-995b-6f89f3b94ef4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d21f13a-49f5-5984-995b-6f89f3b94ef4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474603} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b4b6cfc-23cb-5eb0-8919-b43d591ffb35" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186475227} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca9a59df-fa84-52b0-a9af-915827efaab3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474604} {:answer/id #uuid "728b0d74-df98-5671-8d8a-5feb2fee7585" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca9a59df-fa84-52b0-a9af-915827efaab3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474604} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b9a7b66-659a-52f4-b09c-d7dfb3a71752" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186475228} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a70b8618-1124-58d3-aa2b-c75dbbbd263e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474606} {:answer/id #uuid "2d8c1e5d-ca08-593b-894a-f2013c2bff6b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d8c1e5d-ca08-593b-894a-f2013c2bff6b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474607} :answer-field/id #uuid "2144d32e-05df-5b66-b1e9-b0f76373caaf" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186475229}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "78f9226d-96f1-55af-96d5-28d4a76505e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-183533" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $4\\,|\\,x$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ $x$ is composite\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n- **I.** Whenever $4\\,|\\,x,$ then $x$ is composite\n- **II.** $4\\,|\\,x$ whenever $x$ is composite\n- **III.** $x$ is composite, provided that $4\\,|\\,x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $P⇒Q$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- Whenever $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $Q$ whenever $P$\n\n- $Q,$ provided that $P$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n\\text{Whenever}\\,{{4\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{P(x)},\\,\\text{then}\\,{{x\\text{ is composite}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n{{4\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{whenever}\\,{{x\\text{ is composite}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is composite,}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{provided that}\\,{{4\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id 17592186421149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186198284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b24ae815-5706-5b65-bab8-2d67f8405c9c" :knowledge-point/title "\"Whenever\", and \"Provided That\""}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4af447c-137a-5206-8f45-b1d092bcb140" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474608} {:answer/id #uuid "ab8c70f1-dcc6-5193-8f60-c456fab1f222" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab8c70f1-dcc6-5193-8f60-c456fab1f222" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474609} :answer-field/id #uuid "37d6042b-bd9e-5bc2-bf5e-088b73f1ee19" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186475230} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ffbb1415-92c3-5383-a457-97467be78458" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474610} {:answer/id #uuid "e54dd938-883f-5763-8889-7d44c7efebd1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e54dd938-883f-5763-8889-7d44c7efebd1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474611} :answer-field/id #uuid "510e11c1-b41d-553e-8bcf-6157c3864da3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186475231} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db3d1a4c-e145-5052-9166-f2dc3a5855b4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474612} {:answer/id #uuid "191feb80-41a6-5c7c-9bfd-eaf0a3ee0b7b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186474613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db3d1a4c-e145-5052-9166-f2dc3a5855b4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186474612} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b27cae4-f905-5d73-a66b-12ab5e154ca9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186475232}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7bd7ef2d-fe07-5622-9cee-22e524115939" :question/math-academy-id "q-183566" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x=0$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ ${x}^{2}=x$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n- **I.** Whenever $x=0,$ then ${x}^{2}=x$\n- **II.** ${x}^{2}=x$ whenever $x=0$\n- **III.** $x=0,$ provided that ${x}^{2}=x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $P⇒Q$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- Whenever $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $Q$ whenever $P$\n\n- $Q,$ provided that $P$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n\\text{Whenever}\\,{{x=0\\text{,}}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{then}\\,{{{x}^{2}=x}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n{{{x}^{2}=x}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{whenever}\\,{{x=0}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n{{x=0\\text{,}}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{provided that}\\,{{{x}^{2}=x}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I  and II only.\""} {:db/id 17592186421235 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186166882 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9a62365-4278-557f-ba76-caa31abe7869" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Flux of a Vector Field Through a Tilted Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03158da1-b1d2-5e08-9fb3-bcf52d0b7ade" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96" :db/id 17592186421175} {:answer/id #uuid "228c1e6f-6068-550e-b050-12aa6caa4351" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id 17592186421178} {:answer/id #uuid "3cae5a31-54ec-52d7-9829-e6f79d0db7b0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-32" :db/id 17592186421186} {:answer/id #uuid "52b6e1b8-f74d-549f-80b2-b5dec0190106" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id 17592186421188} {:answer/id #uuid "974560cd-4e8d-59bd-8077-c163da225937" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-96" :db/id 17592186421207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "974560cd-4e8d-59bd-8077-c163da225937" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-96" :db/id 17592186421207} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f22f763-7742-563a-8020-3b6c5519f8c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186421231}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2f0f5aff-a329-55d0-a382-ebd7a7992774" :question/math-academy-id "q-162548" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,x+1,\\,-y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined in Cartesian coordinates as $z=x-4y+1$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $0\\le y\\le 4.$ Calculate the flux of $F$ through $S$ with respect to the *downward*-pointing unit normal vector $n.$\n\n*Hint: You're given that the fundamental vector product of $S$ with respect to its canonical parametrization is $||{r}_{x}\\times {r}_{y}||=3\\sqrt{2}.$*" :question/worked-solution "If $S$ is an oriented surface with unit normal vector $n,$ and $F$ is continuous vector field, then the flux of $F$ across $S$ measured with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nNotice that our surface $z=x-4y+1$ can be written using the dot product as \n\n$$\n⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩\\cdot {{⟨-1,\\,4,\\,1⟩}_{⏟}}_{-\\overset{~}{n}}=1,\\,\\text{or}\\,⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩\\cdot {{⟨1,\\,-4,\\,-1⟩}_{⏟}}_{\\overset{~}{n}}=-1.\n$$\n\nSince we require a downward-pointing normal vector to our surface $S,$ we must select one where the $z$-component is negative. This gives us the normal vector\n\n$$\n\\overset{~}{n}=⟨1,\\,-4,\\,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nNormalizing this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{\\overset{~}{n}}{‖\\overset{~}{n}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{⟨1,\\,-4,\\,-1⟩}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{18}}⟨1,\\,-4,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,\\,-4,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $z=x-4y+1$ on $S,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\cdot n & =⟨z,\\,x+1,\\,-y⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,\\,-4,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}⟨x-4y+1,\\,x+1,\\,-y⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-4,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}(x-4y+1-4(x+1)+y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}(-3x-3y-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(-x-y-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the flux of $F$ across $S$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(-x-y-1)\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(-x-y-1)\\cdot ||{r}_{x}\\times {r}_{y}||\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(-x-y-1)\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}}}(-x-y-1)\\cdot 3\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-3{∬}_{D}(x+y+1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-3{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(x+y+1)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-3{\\int }_{0}^{4}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+xy+x]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-3{\\int }_{0}^{4}(2y+4)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-3[{y}^{2}+4y]_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 32 \\\\  & =-96\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186421237 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186166882 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9a62365-4278-557f-ba76-caa31abe7869" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Flux of a Vector Field Through a Tilted Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33f99146-c5ea-58b5-9bc1-58895cc4fc3f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id 17592186421183} {:answer/id #uuid "351f00b6-bf80-5f84-ad64-40be3bbe2fd6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/id 17592186421184} {:answer/id #uuid "5e434de3-deea-53ed-838e-cf948a5ae65a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id 17592186421192} {:answer/id #uuid "74c21c89-a987-5d09-9152-140d29002bac" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id 17592186421198} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb7492c-b0fb-5b7c-a8dc-51bc27779fe3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id 17592186421200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "351f00b6-bf80-5f84-ad64-40be3bbe2fd6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/id 17592186421184} :answer-field/id #uuid "27f85e1d-9f83-541a-b342-23041c17ed8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186421227}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "49459c91-bfac-5582-aa3d-bc1bfea60a7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-162157" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z+x,\\,x+y,\\,2x+6⟩$ and a finite region $S$ of the plane $z=-x+2y$ such that $\\text{Area}(S)=2\\sqrt{3}.$ Calculate the flux of $F$ through $S$ with respect to the upward-pointing unit normal vector $n.$" :question/worked-solution "If $S$ is an oriented surface with unit normal vector $n,$ and $F$ is continuous vector field, then the flux of $F$ across $S$ measured with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nNotice that our surface $z=-x+2y$ can be written using the dot product as \n\n$$\n⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩\\cdot {{⟨1,\\,-2,\\,1⟩}_{⏟}}_{\\overset{~}{n}}=0,\\,\\text{or}\\,⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩\\cdot {{⟨-1,\\,2,\\,-1⟩}_{⏟}}_{-\\overset{~}{n}}=0.\n$$\n\nSince we require an upward-pointing normal vector to our surface $S,$ we must select one where the $z$-component is positive. This gives us the normal vector\n\n$$\n\\overset{~}{n}=⟨1,\\,-2,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nNormalizing this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{\\overset{~}{n}}{‖\\overset{~}{n}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{⟨1,\\,-2,\\,1⟩}{\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨1,\\,-2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $z=-x+2y$ on $S,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\cdot n & =⟨z+x,\\,x+y,\\,2x+6⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨1,\\,-2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨2y,\\,x+y,\\,2x+6⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}(2y-2(x+y)+2x+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the flux of $F$ across $S$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\text{Area}(S) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186421241 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186166882 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9a62365-4278-557f-ba76-caa31abe7869" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Flux of a Vector Field Through a Tilted Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55f614dd-3b95-57de-8bba-fbdf8531494d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id 17592186421189} {:answer/id #uuid "6ee0e41b-d6ea-5017-8c8a-6f46a0e3dbdb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id 17592186421196} {:answer/id #uuid "8a6976ed-177a-5352-84ae-a730d2e02dc6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id 17592186421203} {:answer/id #uuid "bdd1bd4e-9eca-533a-bc90-7301652e24d6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id 17592186421212} {:answer/id #uuid "dcd79be2-e35a-5ca5-821c-28d7b26f68a1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id 17592186421219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdd1bd4e-9eca-533a-bc90-7301652e24d6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id 17592186421212} :answer-field/id #uuid "be4704df-0892-5011-9881-9914abd2c673" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186421232}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "aa928e5a-70af-5b00-a980-606761f10bda" :question/math-academy-id "q-161243" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x,\\,2y,\\,2z-x-y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined in Cartesian coordinates as $z=x-\\frac{y}{2}+3$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 1.$ Calculate the flux of $F$ through $S$ with respect to the *downward*-pointing unit normal vector $n.$\n\n*Hint: You're given that the fundamental vector product of $S$ with respect to its canonical parametrization is $||{r}_{x}\\times {r}_{y}||=\\frac{3}{2}.$*" :question/worked-solution "If $S$ is an oriented surface with unit normal vector $n,$ and $F$ is continuous vector field, then the flux of $F$ across $S$ measured with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nNotice that our surface $z=x-\\frac{y}{2}+3$ can be written using the dot product as \n\n$$\n⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩\\cdot {{⟨-1,\\,\\frac{1}{2},\\,1⟩}_{⏟}}_{-\\overset{~}{n}}=3,\\,\\text{or}\\,⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩\\cdot {{⟨1,\\,-\\frac{1}{2},\\,-1⟩}_{⏟}}_{\\overset{~}{n}}=-3.\n$$\n\nSince we require a downward-pointing normal vector to our surface $S,$ we must select one where the $z$-component is negative. This gives us the normal vector\n\n$$\n\\overset{~}{n}=⟨1,\\,-\\frac{1}{2},\\,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nNormalizing this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{\\overset{~}{n}}{‖\\overset{~}{n}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{⟨1,\\,-\\frac{1}{2},\\,-1⟩}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}⟨1,\\,-\\frac{1}{2},\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $z=x-\\frac{y}{2}+3$ on $S,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\cdot n & =⟨x,\\,2y,\\,2z-x-y⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}⟨2,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨x,\\,2y,\\,(2x-y+6)-x-y⟩\\cdot ⟨2,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨x,\\,2y,\\,x-2y+6⟩\\cdot ⟨2,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(2x-2y-2(x-2y+6)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(2y-12).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the flux of $F$ across $S$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\frac{1}{3}(2y-12)\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{3}(2y-12)\\cdot ||{r}_{x}\\times {r}_{y}||\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{3}(2y-12)\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{1}{\\cancel{3}}(2y-12)\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{3}}{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(y-6)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(y-6)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{-1}^{1}(y-6)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[x]_{0}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-6y]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-12) \\\\  & =-24\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186422737 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186157254 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff0294bf-aed0-529b-98bc-ea5983c7e262" :knowledge-point/title "Proving a Linear Expression Is Even"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c892d9c-d7e6-5fc8-a99c-cac62c97c0d7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2b-a" :db/id 17592186422508} {:answer/id #uuid "3a51a4aa-58c5-5528-b7fd-2a2148b8ad77" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2a" :db/id 17592186422531} {:answer/id #uuid "3baee206-d3de-54b3-a0c5-baf5169924be" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2a+1" :db/id 17592186422532} {:answer/id #uuid "4f7d6afc-68e9-576e-9b48-a676f00123f6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2b+1" :db/id 17592186422552} {:answer/id #uuid "f141f29d-611a-