id #uuid "88cb35a9-70ec-5207-82cf-00d64d8ca03e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3a+1" :db/id 17592186422590} {:answer/id #uuid "ac61db7a-7166-562c-823f-bdaf7b202ee2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(9a)" :db/id 17592186422616} {:answer/id #uuid "dbb45d51-aa75-5270-b658-2985119bd792" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(9a)+1" :db/id 17592186422658} {:answer/id #uuid "defa5177-faee-5622-acaf-9d7006be2790" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(3a+1)" :db/id 17592186422661} {:answer/id #uuid "e1ef7bed-5eaa-55a3-8d02-381e23ac320f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(9a+1)" :db/id 17592186422664} {:answer/id #uuid "f5595efa-0b65-53bf-a0ce-be2822b74bdc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9a" :db/id 17592186422677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5595efa-0b65-53bf-a0ce-be2822b74bdc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9a" :db/id 17592186422677} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc0855dd-1d56-55a1-9092-50acbc482061" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id 17592186422735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "777be974-f06f-56a1-8838-5bb4b1e9b194" :question/math-academy-id "q-184291" :question/problem "Prove that  $9n-8$ is odd if $n$ is an odd integer.\n\nLet $n$ be an odd integer. Then, $n=\\,${{field-1}} for some integer $a.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9n-8 & ={{field-2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $b=$ {{field-3}}. Since $a$ is {{field-4}}, we have that $b$ is {{field-5}}.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9n-8 & ={{field-6}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is one larger than a multiple of $2.$ Therefore, $9n-8$ is {{field-7}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- If an integer $n$ is even, then there exists an integer $p$ such that $n=2p.$\n\n- If an integer $n$ is odd, then there exists an integer $q$ such that $n=2q+1.$\n\nIn this case, we need to show the following:\n\n$$\nn\\text{ is odd}\\,⇒\\,9n-8\\text{ is odd}\n$$\n\nWe start by using the fact that $n$ is odd.\n\nLet $n$ be an odd integer. Then, $n=2a+1$ for some integer $a.$\n\nThe idea is to substitute $n=2a+1$ into our expression $9n-8$ and show it is odd by writing it as a multiple of $2,$ plus $1.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9n-8 & =9(2a+1)-8 \\\\  & =18a+9-8 \\\\  & =2{{(9a)}_{⏟}}_{b}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we define another integer $b=9a$ (highlighted above), we have that $9n-8=2b+1,$ which shows that $9n-8$ is indeed one more than a multiple of $2.$\n\nLet $b=9a.$ Since $a$ is an integer, we have that $b$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9n-8 & =2{{(9a)}_{⏟}}_{b}+1 \\\\  & =2b+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is one larger than a multiple of $2.$ \n\nFinally, we write our conclusion.\n\nTherefore, $9n-8$ is odd."} {:db/id 17592186422741 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186157255 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2ec1dc-7365-5ba6-bc6d-6e9a13a29cd0" :knowledge-point/title "Proving a Linear Expression Is Odd"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1121103d-07e9-5063-b94e-cfeb51cc70ae" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2a" :db/id 17592186422504} {:answer/id #uuid "13ff42a5-d7ce-5a98-b0b1-c2e3029de743" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2b" :db/id 17592186422506} {:answer/id #uuid "59fb5323-46a5-587d-b734-4ba9516d55a3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2a+1" :db/id 17592186422560} {:answer/id #uuid "9bc3f142-3aca-55ec-9553-fc80a22aeca2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498