 }_{1}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $3$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."} {:db/id 17592186551310 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186133804 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "950c1ed7-f804-54f5-bf97-16bf2d1a663b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Least-Squares Regression Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3414a2fb-1c40-5baf-b160-d62aa452c159" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-2+4x" :db/id 17592186550495} {:answer/id #uuid "580265ce-7676-517c-8e36-74524881eba6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2-4x" :db/id 17592186550583} {:answer/id #uuid "6f203b32-367e-5763-8e6c-d666dfea11ee" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4-2x" :db/id 17592186550646} {:answer/id #uuid "b301229a-92bc-5022-a48f-18260e3a02d2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2+4x" :db/id 17592186550855} {:answer/id #uuid "e41db3bb-d1d9-5070-ae1b-2af09a13aaa7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4+2x" :db/id 17592186550990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f203b32-367e-5763-8e6c-d666dfea11ee" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4-2x" :db/id 17592186550646} :answer-field/id #uuid "b80c480a-b5ef-5b14-b066-cb5d8f7268c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186551178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "95655e19-4263-5e26-a218-4871ce1b1f2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-139645" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$-3$** | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $9$ | $6$ | $3$ | $-2$ |\n\nFind the line of the form $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above.\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that*\n\n$$\n({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{56}[\\begin{aligned}14 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{X}^{T}y=[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -28\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n*where $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector.*" :question/worked-solution "The coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by ${X}^{T},$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\n{X}^{T}\\,X\\hat{\\beta }={X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\hat{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values of $({X}^{T}X)^{-1}$ and ${X}^{T}y$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{\\beta } & =({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}\\,y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{56}[\\begin{aligned}14 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -28\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $y=4-2x.$"} {:db/id 17592186551332 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186133905 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6acfe386-f7e4-54b1-9701-6ff5905b4536" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements of a Regression Line in Terms of Matrices and Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0296fe2c-3620-54f1-9ba1-56fc76e2a57d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186550378} {:answer/id #uuid "7835779c-d98b-5054-95c1-feb0292ef6ee" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186550673} {:answer/id #uuid "962f0311-8a0a-531a-b2a4-eb199b394c72" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -4 & -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186550749} {:answer/id #uuid "a2030c00-81cb-582d-8ab1-8b808a0ea7d7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186550786} {:answer/id #uuid "f3177ddd-2ea5-5752-a73b-5a4850d40c00" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -4 & -2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186551019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0296fe2c-3620-54f1-9ba1-56fc76e2a57d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186550378} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c2c5892-f74c-576d-86e2-c3d98f1ea70e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186551159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c02b9ef4-844a-58b2-be01-9b59908adb2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-139574" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$-6$** | **$-4$** | **$-2$** | **$0$** | **$2$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $5$ | $8$ | $11$ | $15$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients  of the line $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above can be found using linear regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$-6$** | **$-4$** | **$-2$** | **$0$** | **$2$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $5$ | $8$ | $11$ | $15$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 11 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."} {:db/id 17592186551337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186133805 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd286741-bf82-5723-a9c1-acf7a8b238c2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Least-Squares Regression Line in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0334f116-416e-5d14-b3bf-b66d4f75de11" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8.25$  points per game" :db/id 17592186550380} {:answer/id #uuid "33db2298-5797-5cb1-af3d-bf806c19e083" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7.75$  points per game" :db/id 17592186550493} {:answer/id #uuid "bd226916-bde7-517b-871e-7e8629dd5812" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$  points per game" :db/id 17592186550887} {:answer/id #uuid "d2b10de6-86fa-53ca-94d7-3e008b6bfb17" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$9$  points per game" :db/id 17592186550935} {:answer/id #uuid "f5961ae6-fa3a-550a-9ffb-b71a8701df1f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8.75$  points per game" :db/id 17592186551025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd226916-bde7-517b-871e-7e8629dd5812" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$  points per game" :db/id 17592186550887} :answer-field/id #uuid "5784eef9-0ad2-5040-8dd4-135f8ec74797" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186551117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d6dbf98c-84c4-5c67-a15a-4f405cbbd0b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-41401" :question/problem "The height (in feet) and the average number of points scored per game (APG) of four players on a basketball team are shown in the following table. \n\n| Height $(x)$ | **$6$** | **$6.5$** | **$6.5$** | **$7$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| APG $(y)$ | $5$ | $8$ | $10$ | $10$ |\n\nFind the line of the form $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above. According to the model, what will be the average number of points scored per game by a player whose height is $6.45\\,\\text{ft}?$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that*\n\n$$\n({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}84.75 & -13 \\\\ -13 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{X}^{T}y=[\\begin{aligned}33 \\\\ 217\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n*where $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector.*" :question/worked-solution "The coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 6.5 \\\\ 1 & 6.5 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by ${X}^{T},$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\n{X}^{T}\\,X\\hat{\\beta }={X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\hat{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\n \n\nSubstituting the given values of $({X}^{T}X)^{-1}$ and ${X}^{T}y$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{\\beta } & =({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}\\,y \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}84.75 & -13 \\\\ -13 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}33 \\\\ 217\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-24.25 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the line $y=-24.25+5x.$ \n\nFinally, to predict the average number of points scored per game by a player whose height is $6.45\\,\\text{ft},$  we substitute $x=6.45$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-24.25+5(6.45) \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, according to the model,  the average number of points scored per game by a player whose height is $6.45\\,\\text{ft}$ will be $8$  points per game."} {:db/id 17592186551340 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186133823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa5bf185-de29-5185-ba57-c64250332dfa" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Elements of a Polynomial Regression Model"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "625975e6-7869-5a67-bc59-519fa2d8371d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186550604} {:answer/id #uuid "65dd863d-70c0-5170-aa9a-00b0ab5e1a31" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(-5)^{2} \\\\ (-25)^{2} \\\\ {5}^{2} \\\\ {20}^{2} \\\\ {35}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186550618} {:answer/id #uuid "a348d2b4-ce93-5a99-a6ed-1906d407475a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}(-3)^{2} \\\\ (-1)^{2} \\\\ {1}^{2} \\\\ {3}^{2} \\\\ {5}^{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186550791} {:answer/id #uuid "a61433c9-2b22-57c8-9478-14e323e7d6b6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -25 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 35\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186550804} {:answer/id #uuid "a6559ef5-d440-5051-9b33-5e541b8f53b5" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186550805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a61433c9-2b22-57c8-9478-14e323e7d6b6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -25 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 35\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186550804} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4aab56a-66ce-5d92-bf05-9bff500864c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186551175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 1759218604548