5$** | **$22$** | **$28$** |\n| $y$ | $-10$ | $-3$ | $5$ | $14$ | $24$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the plane \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}{x}_{1}+{\\beta }_{2}{x}_{2}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 15 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 22 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 28\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector."} {:db/id 17592186552468 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186133809 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eaee4e9-7be5-5c35-bc88-89697a15d75a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements of a Multiple Linear Regression That Passes Through the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d7f0998-e9d5-5406-9a4c-938cd37e78b8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186551816} {:answer/id #uuid "45a14343-4d9a-5422-8de7-7fea93595715" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 15 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 25 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 31 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 40\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186551835} {:answer/id #uuid "8c7fe0d0-0f24-5eee-949c-be0cf29ab0f3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 15 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 19 & 9 \\\\ 3 & 25 & 13 \\\\ 4 & 31 & 25 \\\\ 5 & 40 & 27\\end{aligned}]" :db/id 17592186552007} {:answer/id #uuid "aa1a6015-a345-5f0a-bf3a-6dc46a45bebc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 15 \\